AB  - A speckled dolphin Sousa plumbea was caught in a fisherman''s net in Kurasini Creek, Dar es Salaam [Tanzania] Dec. 29, 1971. The sex of this animal, which had a 62.5 kg body wt and 191 cm overall length, was not determined. The skull is figured. A male long-beaked dolphin, Stenella longirostris (Gray), was found dead floating in water near the entrance to Dar es Salaam harbor. The skull had an overall length of 199 cm. Each testis measured .apprx. 10 .times. 2 cm. Numerous nematodes (Anisakis simplex) were found in the esophagus and stomach.
